  "id": "t03-005",
  "track": "track-03",
  "title": "aggregation grouping and window functions",
  "status": "source-backed-scope-complete",
  "concepts": [
    "WHERE filters rows before grouping; GROUP BY forms groups and HAVING filters groups after aggregation. NULL and empty-input behavior differs among aggregate functions.",
    "GROUPING SETS, ROLLUP, and CUBE compute multiple subtotal levels; GROUPING metadata distinguishes subtotal placeholders from data NULLs.",
    "Window functions retain rows while evaluating over a partition, order, and frame. The frame is not the same as the partition, and defaults can produce surprising peer behavior.",
    "Ranking, offset, distribution, and aggregate windows answer different questions. A window ORDER BY does not define final result order."
  ],
